      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a 4-year-old and 42lb child, the typical dosage of Children's Tylenol liquid (acetaminophen) is 160mg per 5mL, but you should refer to the dosage chart on the bottle. It's generally safe to give 160-320mg (5-10mL) every 4-6 hours but consult your pediatrician for a personalized dosage. If his fever is lower than 102°F or it's been less than 4 hours since he last took it, you may consider not repeating yet. Always consult with a healthcare professional if in doubt.",
